{#
    The focused single-task shell: sign in, password reset, email confirmation, the forced
    password change (FR-001, FR-004, FR-005, FR-006).

    One card, centred on the dark canvas, with the platform mark above it — the design's auth
    surface. No navigation, and that is the point on two of these pages:

      - A signed-out visitor has nowhere to navigate to.
      - A user carrying `must_change_password` is redirected back here from every other route
         (FR-006), so a sidebar would be a list of links that all bounce.

    The context switcher is deliberately absent for the same reason: it changes what every
    subsequent page shows, and on these pages there is no subsequent page yet.

    Heading structure: the card's own `<h1>` is the page heading, so a screen-reader user landing
    here hears the task first. `#main-content` is on the `<main>` so the skip link in
    `base.html.twig` has its target on these pages too.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block body_class %}pp-theme{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <main id="main-content" class="pp-auth">
        {#
            Not a link. The only thing above a sign-in form worth linking to would be a marketing
            site this application does not have, and a logo that navigates to the demo route
            index is a trap rather than a wayfinder.
        #}
        <p class="pp-brand">
            <span class="pp-brand-mark">{{ include('_logo.html.twig') }}</span>
            <span>{{ app_name }}</span>
        </p>

        <div class="pp-auth-card">
            <div class="pp-auth-head">
                <h1 class="pp-auth-title">{% block heading %}{% endblock %}</h1>
                {% block lead %}{% endblock %}
            </div>

            {# Flash messages announce themselves to assistive tech without stealing focus. #}
            <div role="status" aria-live="polite">
                {% for label, messages in app.flashes %}
                    {% for message in messages %}
                        <p class="flash flash-{{ label }}">{{ message }}</p>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

            {% block account_content %}{% endblock %}
        </div>
    </main>
{% endblock %}
